# VITE_API_URL: Base URL of the FastAPI backend (no /api suffix).
#
# Unset:
#   - `npm run dev` calls http://localhost:8000.
#   - A production build calls the origin it is served from. That is right when
#     the backend serves dist/ (FRONTEND_DIST), but on a static host (Vercel,
#     Netlify, ...) it points at the static site itself, so detection requests
#     fail with "Cannot reach the backend" / "Unexpected response" until a
#     backend URL is set: either build with VITE_API_URL, or have the visitor
#     enter one in the Demo's API Config panel.
#
# Set it when the backend lives somewhere else. It is baked in at build time, so
# change it and rebuild. The backend must be reachable over HTTPS from an HTTPS
# page, and its CORS_ORIGINS must include the site's origin.
# VITE_API_URL="https://your-backend.example.com"
